now from a big premiere to a huge  series finale as post bids farewell  after three seasons  this is it  this is the end the critically acclaimed  show which focused on the lives of trans  women and gay men of color during the  eighth epidemic  held a finale celebration at the fyc  panel on saturday in pasadena california  stars billy porter mj rodriguez  co-creators ryan murphy  steven canals and two huge super fans  elton john and david furnish  all attended the drive-in event this  series touched me more than any other  series because  of the journey that these people are on  i mean i am  electra i  [Music]  while of course there were laughs the  final episode also brought tears as  billy's character lost his battle  with aids i'm not ready to lose you pray  [Music]  i'm not ready to let go a poignant  moment for the show and billy as just  last month he opened up for the first  time about his real-life battle with hiv  after being diagnosed 14 years ago at  the event david furnish noted that while  there's been progress in treating hiv  and aids  the fight isn't over the medicines are  so effective now that we're not seeing  people sick and dying  thank god they work really really well  but we have frightening statistics  like in america 50 percent of all  gay black men in america will contract  hiv in their lifetime  and with the medicines that we have  today if everybody knew about hiv  knew they were at risk and had access to  testing and treatment  we could stop this disease dead in its  tracks
 

